From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:42:17 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 277/297] Meridian: "Try with Claude" opens a page that loads

"Give this site a new look" on an empty tab opened the first website at
CERN, whose certificate expired: the person saw "Your connection is not
private". Each card now has a list of plain pages, best first, and opens
the first that answers (HEAD, no cookies, 4 s, all at once):
meridianbrowser.app/demo/plain.html, then paulgraham.com and danluu.com
to restyle; Hacker News, then text.npr.org to critique. Tests name the
pages that "answer" with --meridian-reachable-urls (no network).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
